==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|lacquey}} (verb only)

===Etymology===
{{etyl|frm|en}} {{m|frm|laquais}}, which is probably (via {{etyl|pro|en}} {{m|pro|lacai}}?) from {{etyl|es|en}} {{m|es|lacayo}}, itself perhaps from {{etyl|it|en}} {{m|it|lacchè}} and {{etyl|el|en}} {{m|el|λακές}}, from {{etyl|tr|en}} {{m|tr|ulak}}. Another possibility is through {{etyl|fr|en}}, from {{etyl|ca|en}} {{m|ca|alacay}}, from {{etyl|ar|en}} {{m|ar|قَاضٍ|اَلْقَاضِي|magistrate}}. See French {{m|fr|laquais}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlæ.ki/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|æki|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[footman]], a [[livery|liveried]] male servant.
# A [[fawn|fawning]], servile follower; a [[lickspittle]].

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|lackey caterpillar}}
* {{l|en|lackey moth}}

